    "M010799": {
      "causal_reason": "The generator changes from 20 random bytes (160 bits) to 21 random bytes (168 bits). The amount of entropy, raw-key length, Base32 enrollment string length and wrapped-ciphertext length therefore change; these outputs are not claimed bit-identical. The released contract is a fresh strong shared secret provisioned as opaque unpadded Base32, with the same HMAC-SHA1, six digits, 30-second step, past/current verification and authenticated at-rest wrapping. Neither the public TotpSetupResponse schema, portal enrollment/QR flow, User storage nor the verifier imposes a 20-byte secret width. Both variants retain at least the 160-bit recommended entropy and interoperate through actual HTTP setup, enable, login, recovery and replacement as well as independent HMAC and native AES-GCM checks. RFC4226 requires at least 128 bits and recommends 160; RFC6238 recommends HMAC-output-length keys for interoperability, rather than declaring other key lengths invalid. The None variant uses the documented default-length secrets API, with fresh native CSPRNG and full uncached backend mypy checks passing. This review is bound to the recorded interpreter and supported enrollment contract; it does not promise an arbitrary future stdlib default or unchanged manual-entry length. Prior exact20 mock assertions, and the mock TypeError on the supported None argument, are withdrawn.",
